1
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,700
Know ye the land where the cypress and myrtle

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,820
Are emblems of deeds that are done in their clime?

3
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:11,900
Where the rage of the vulture, the love of the turtle,

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:16,400
Now melt into sorrow, now madden to crime?

5
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,420
Know ye the land of the cedar and vine,

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:23,000
Where the flowers ever blossom, the beams ever shine;

7
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:26,520
Where the light wings of Zephyr, oppressed with perfume,

8
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,560
Wax faint o'er the gardens of Gúl in her bloom;

9
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:34,500
Where the citron and olive are fairest of fruit,

10
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,960
And the voice of the nightingale never is mute;

11
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,720
Where the tints of the earth, and the hues of the sky,

12
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,680
In colour though varied, in beauty may vie,

13
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:47,020
And the purple of Ocean is deepest in dye;

14
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,560
Where the virgins are soft as the roses they twine,

15
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:54,380
And all, save the spirit of man, is divine—

16
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,880
'Tis the clime of the East—'tis the land of the Sun—

17
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:02,620
Can he smile on such deeds as his children have done?

18
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,740
Oh! wild as the accents of lovers' farewell

19
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,720
Are the hearts which they bear, and the tales which they tell.

